; worldscratch.eval — run INSIDE a freshly created world (W7).
;
; Launched with `-project wt_scratch`, which is how a test scenario gets its own
; world without touching settings.ini. Two things are worth reading: the world
; that is open is the one named on the command line, and a world made by
; `worlds new` passes the checker as it stands — content copied across, places
; and the hooks that name them left behind.
logecho on
; `reset` opens the game where a new one would - which for a world made
; by `worlds new` is its starter room, because creating one names it as
; the harness level. Without this the run sits at the title screen and
; `validate` answers "only works in-game", which is what the first
; version of this script did.
reset
worlds
levels
validate
